+# Roadmap — 30 days from 2026-07-08
+
+Companion to `2026-07-08-mirror.md`. Rule inherited from the analysis:
+insight without a next action is entertainment.
+
+**The one metric:** by **Tue 2026-08-05**, the first real user (a 25-year IP attorney)
+completes one unit of real work in `apps/oip-web` — opens it, does something the
+practice needs, without hand-holding.
+
+---
+
+## This week (Jul 8–15) — DROP and WIRE
+
+- [ ] Uninstall the dead tool trials (Grok CLI, opencode, openclaw, zen-mcp).
+      Law from the record: a tool that doesn't hit 20 typed prompts in week one never
+      revives. Next shiny CLI gets an eval-agent report, not a weekend.
+- [ ] Install the anti-tax tooling: `/packet-run`, `/lesson`, `/demo-day`,
+      1Password preflight hook.
+- [ ] **Cap the ratchet.** Standards inventories hit zero 2026-07-08 (#340).
+      Platform work is maintenance-only (red CI, real bugs, security) until the
+      Aug 5 metric is met. Every ratchet click past zero is polish on armor.
+- [ ] **Thursday Jul 9: Demo Day #1.** One user-visible increment of oip-web,
+      shown to the user. Tiny is fine. Visible is mandatory.
+
+## Weeks 2–4 (Jul 16 – Aug 5) — DELEGATE and AIM
+
+- [ ] PR shepherding goes autonomous (~3 hrs/wk back): scheduled morning agent runs
+      yeet monitor to merge-readiness; pings only on true blockers.
+- [ ] Packet drafting goes agent-first (~2 hrs/wk back): detector output →
+      agent-drafted packet → human edit. Judgment stays; transcription goes.
+- [ ] Research goes on cron (~2 hrs/wk back): recurring deep-research runs land
+      cited reports in the research directory on a schedule.
+- [ ] Thursdays Jul 16 / 23 / 30: Demo Days #2–4. The record says Thursday runs at
+      2× Monday volume. Ride the wave; point it outward. Four demos = a user habit
+      by August.
+
+## Daily — PROTECT (the calendar obeys the timestamps)
+
+- **23:00–03:00 — design only.** Measured best window (schema-work at 3.4× the daytime
+  rate). Architecture, modeling, packet-writing. Never ops.
+- **~14:00 — dispatch window.** Secondary peak. Kick fleets here so results are waiting
+  at midnight. Scheduled agents run without a human trigger.
+- **10:00–12:00 — trough.** Admin only. Never schedule thinking here.
+- **Never delegate the challenging.** Adversarial verification of agent claims stays
+  a human job. It's the moat against vibe slop.
+
+## FOCUS — the two things only you can do
+
+1. **Decomposition into worker-safe lanes** — the rarest skill in the archive, and
+   exactly what the agentic-OS-for-professionals product is made of. It counts only
+   when it ships inside the product.
+2. **The family IP-practice corpus** — a 25-year practice, a willing expert user,
+   ontology chops. Nobody else has this asset. Platform polish is replaceable labor;
+   oip.law is not.
+
+## KEEP — working systems, don't touch
+
+- goals/ packets + yeet loop (receipts: five PRs merged within days of each other).
+- Adversarial verification rounds.
+- Scope-contract prompt style (why the fleets don't go rogue).
+- The midnight block itself.
+
+## Scoreboard (fill in weekly, honestly)
+
+| Week | Demo shipped? | User touched it? | Ratchet clicks past zero | Hours in dispatch |
+|------|---------------|------------------|--------------------------|-------------------|
+| Jul 9 | | | | |
+| Jul 16 | | | | |
+| Jul 23 | | | | |
+| Jul 30 | | | | |
+| Aug 5 → **metric met?** | | | | |
+
+If three weeks pass with demos shipped but the ratchet column climbing and the user
+column empty: reread the mirror. The wall rebuilds itself quietly. That's what it's for.
